n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(11{e}^{x}+8{x}^{2}-12x-20) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(11{e}^{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8{x}^{2})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(12x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(20) \\\\  & =11\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})+8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})-12\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(20) \\\\  & =11{e}^{x}+8(2x)-12(1)-0 \\\\  & =11{e}^{x}+16x-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=0$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=0} & ={(11{e}^{x}+16x-12)|}_{x=0} \\\\  & =11{e}^{0}+16\\cdot 0-12 \\\\  & =11\\cdot 1+0-12 \\\\  & =11-12 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245266 1000 #edb/ref 17592186245267 13194139533665 true] [17592186245266 1000 #edb/ref 17592186245268 13194139533665 true] [17592186245266 1000 #edb/ref 17592186245269 13194139533665 true] [17592186245266 1000 #edb/ref 17592186245270 13194139533665 true] [17592186245266 1000 #edb/ref 17592186245271 13194139533665 true] [17592186245266 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533665 true] [17592186245266 1041 "selection" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245266 1104 #edb/ref 17592186245270 13194139533665 true] [17592186245266 1110 #uuid "7da4826b-5ec3-5f81-954a-7e77adbd899c" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245267 1034 "1" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245267 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533665 true] [17592186245267 1111 #uuid "9533f672-1273-558b-976a-c9808d9634f4" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245268 1034 "-3" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245268 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533665 true] [17592186245268 1111 #uuid "d75aa0e5-48ff-51c7-88b7-5d17442e535b" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245269 1034 "0" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245269 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533665 true] [17592186245269 1111 #uuid "ba8507fc-287c-595a-868d-23c80652e40c" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245270 1034 "-1" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245270 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533665 true] [17592186245270 1111 #uuid "5c3b7e2b-79a6-5680-8e90-5524874769b9" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245271 1034 "5" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245271 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533665 true] [17592186245271 1111 #uuid "f589d543-7898-53f0-966c-016fce897ef7" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245272 1017 #edb/ref 17592186245273 13194139533665 true] [17592186245272 1089 "q-17388" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245272 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533665 true] [17592186245272 1100 "Given that $f(x)={3}^{x}+5{e}^{x}$, find the instantaneous rate of change at $x=0.$" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245272 1113 #uuid "d4297003-d87d-50b1-8d62-c56588831177" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245272 1138 false 13194139533665 true] [17592186245272 1145 "Applying the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({3}^{x}+5{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({3}^{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}(5{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({3}^{x})+5\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x}) \\\\  & ={3}^{x}ln⁡3+5{e}^{x}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change at $x=0$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=0} & ={({3}^{x}ln⁡3+5{e}^{x})|}_{x=0} \\\\  & ={3}^{0}ln⁡3+5{e}^{0} \\\\  & =1\\cdot ln⁡3+5\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =ln⁡3+5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245273 1000 #edb/ref 17592186245274 13194139533665 true] [17592186245273 1000 #edb/ref 17592186245275 13194139533665 true] [17592186245273 1000 #edb/ref 17592186245276 13194139533665 true] [17592186245273 1000 #edb/ref 17592186245277 13194139533665 true] [17592186245273 1000 #edb/ref 17592186245278 13194139533665 true] [17592186245273 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533665 true] [17592186245273 1041 "selection" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245273 1104 #edb/ref 17592186245274 13194139533665 true] [17592186245273 1110 #uuid "e5c9bfd2-6e1c-5078-86fc-2bbc3906ccd5" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245274 1034 "ln⁡3+5" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245274 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533665 true] [17592186245274 1111 #uuid "a8ceeea3-9d41-55e5-b584-5aeb99474063" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245275 1034 "ln⁡3" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245275 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533665 true] [17592186245275 1111 #uuid "edad8190-417a-5069-b8e2-977076c2e1f1" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245276 1034 "ln⁡3+5e" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245276 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533665 true] [17592186245276 1111 #uuid "58f52d14-95ee-582b-bab5-a83eedbbf36c" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245277 1034 "6" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245277 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533665 true] [17592186245277 1111 #uuid "cbfc7296-a450-5ed8-a358-2c4347a0d850" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245278 1034 "5" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245278 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533665 true] [17592186245278 1111 #uuid "f68449a8-1439-54b6-9112-9b071eadd874" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245279 1017 #edb/ref 17592186245280 13194139533665 true] [17592186245279 1089 "q-304035" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245279 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533665 true] [17592186245279 1100 "Given that $f(x)=6{x}^{7}+2{e}^{x}$, the exact value of the slope of the tangent line at $x=-1$ is{{field-1}}." 13194139533665 true] [17592186245279 1113 #uuid "e65e96ca-4822-5bf0-bb2c-1ba7385542a1" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245279 1138 false 13194139533665 true] [17592186245279 1145 "First, using the addition and the power rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6{x}^{7}+2{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6{x}^{7})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =6\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{7})+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x}) \\\\  & =6(7{x}^{6})+2{e}^{x} \\\\  & =42{x}^{6}+2{e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=-1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=-1} & ={(42{x}^{6}+2{e}^{x})\\,|}_{x=-1} \\\\  & =42(-1)^{6}+2{e}^{-1} \\\\  & =42\\cdot 1+\\frac{2}{e} \\\\  & =42+\\frac{2}{e}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245280 1000 #edb/ref 17592186245281 13194139533665 true] [17592186245280 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533665 true] [17592186245280 1041 "field-1" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245280 1104 #edb/ref 17592186245281 13194139533665 true] [17592186245280 1110 #uuid "4e07171e-7a33-53a0-97d2-e7b785679a49" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245281 1034 "42+2e^{-1}" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245281 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533665 true] [17592186245281 1111 #uuid "d96f7801-6943-57f4-b621-19f2d5dcde26" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245282 1017 #edb/ref 17592186245283 13194139533665 true] [17592186245282 1089 "q-304038" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245282 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533665 true] [17592186245282 1100 "Given that $f(x)=3\\cdot {8}^{x}+12x+10$, find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245282 1113 #uuid "bd96388d-6f15-569f-bc11-b254a12e45eb" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245282 1138 false 13194139533665 true] [17592186245282 1145 "Applying the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3\\cdot {8}^{x}+12x+10) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3\\cdot {8}^{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(12x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(10) \\\\  & =3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({8}^{x})+12\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(10) \\\\  & =3(ln⁡(8){8}^{x})+12(1)+0 \\\\  & =3ln⁡(8){8}^{x}+12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245283 1000 #edb/ref 17592186245284 13194139533665 true] [17592186245283 1000 #edb/ref 17592186245285 13194139533665 true] [17592186245283 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533665 true] [17592186245283 1041 "field-1" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245283 1104 #edb/ref 17592186245284 13194139533665 true] [17592186245283 1110 #uuid "e6936770-a4e5-5a11-9389-0331d0fdaf38" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245284 1034 "3\\cdot8^x\\ln(8)+12" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245284 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533665 true] [17592186245284 1111 #uuid "bc271ec7-0efc-54b3-9115-2685575056a3" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245285 1034 "3\\cdot8^x+12" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245285 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533665 true] [17592186245285 1111 #uuid "41681629-b813-58d0-8acb-d3d785c357f9" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245286 1017 #edb/ref 17592186245287 13194139533665 true] [17592186245286 1089 "q-340056" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245286 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533665 true] [17592186245286 1100 "Given that $f(x)=6{e}^{x}+ln⁡8,$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245286 1113 #uuid "5a13ddf1-d3b9-5682-9ec2-7dea245fa36c" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245286 1138 false 13194139533665 true] [17592186245286 1145 "The derivative of ${e}^{x}$ is just ${e}^{x}$ itself. On the other hand, $ln⁡8$ is a constant, so its derivative is $0.$\n\nUsing the addition rule, then, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6{e}^{x}+ln⁡8) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6{e}^{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ln⁡8) \\\\  & =6\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})+0 \\\\  & =6{e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245287 1000 #edb/ref 17592186245288 13194139533665 true] [17592186245287 1000 #edb/ref 17592186245289 13194139533665 true] [17592186245287 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533665 true] [17592186245287 1041 "field-1" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245287 1104 #edb/ref 17592186245288 13194139533665 true] [17592186245287 1110 #uuid "785fb0a2-54cf-5451-8622-411e9884a29a" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245288 1034 "6e^x" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245288 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533665 true] [17592186245288 1111 #uuid "cfc49b76-77a7-546d-a59c-0e938e14c9d7" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245289 1034 "6e^x+8" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245289 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533665 true] [17592186245289 1111 #uuid "43073e84-5690-55fc-ac6a-fa934c6e7fba" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245290 1017 #edb/ref 17592186245291 13194139533665 true] [17592186245290 1089 "q-340067" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245290 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533665 true] [17592186245290 1100 "Given that $f(x)=9{e}^{x}+ln⁡4$, the slope of the tangent line at $x=ln⁡2$ is{{field-1}}." 13194139533665 true] [17592186245290 1113 #uuid "020a6823-fb1e-518f-92c1-a5ae8eb08fe5" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245290 1138 false 13194139533665 true] [17592186245290 1145 "The derivative of ${e}^{x}$ is just ${e}^{x}$ itself. On the other hand, $ln⁡4$ is a constant, so its derivative is $0.$\n\nFirst, using the addition rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(9{e}^{x}+ln⁡4) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(9{e}^{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ln⁡4) \\\\  & =9\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})+0 \\\\  & =9{e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=ln⁡2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=ln⁡2} & ={(9{e}^{x})\\,|}_{x=ln⁡2} \\\\  & =9{e}^{ln⁡2} \\\\  & =9\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245291 1000 #edb/ref 17592186245292 13194139533665 true] [17592186245291 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533665 true] [17592186245291 1041 "field-1" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245291 1104 #edb/ref 17592186245292 13194139533665 true] [17592186245291 1110 #uuid "304b2bbd-9e43-58d4-8a50-05bf8bb76d8e" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245292 1034 "18" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245292 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533665 true] [17592186245292 1111 #uuid "47a48e23-9c46-506c-8e92-391f4fe24039" 13194139533665 true] [17592186245293 1017 #